<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orinoco</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Orinoco River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orinoco is one of the longest rivers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, flowing about 2,140 kilometres from the Guiana Highlands through Venezuela and along the Colombian border to a vast delta on the Atlantic. Its plains, the llanos, were a battleground of the independence wars, and its town of Angostura served as Bolívar's base. Early explorers sought the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-dorado">El Dorado</a> along its course.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orinoco.jpg" alt="Orinoco" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: jkaiser · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orinoco_Bridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
